.TH man 1 "11 August 2025" "1.0" "User Commands"
.SH NAME 
	cpcd - cp a file then cd to where it is
.SH SYNOPSIS
	cpcd destination
.SH DESCRIPTION
	does cp then puts you there. if you specify a dirname, it copies the file there with its current name and cds to that dir.
.br
	if you give a filename, it copies the file to that name then cds to the directory it's in. basically same as cp but yo uend up where the file ends up
.SH OPTIONS
	cp default options work, so -i to prompt before overwrite, -n to not overwrite, -b to make backups, -u for update, -v for verbose. Copies directories by default (-r)
.SH EXAMPLES
	cpcd *.csv csvs
.br
	cpcd sdifji.py ../../ijsdif/jsissbsbbsb.py
.SH BUGS
	probably none
